d what the keyboard fixes require, and any\n  flow outside the four audited ones.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited flows can be completed end-to-end using only the keyboard,\n  verified by a per-flow walkthrough of the audit defect list, with no focus traps and\n  no unreachable controls.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is resolved, or\n  explicitly dispositioned with a recorded reason where the audit item is deemed not a\n  defect.\n- Focus indicators are visible and stylistically consistent across all interactive\n  controls in the audited flows.\n- The Dashboard's existing automated test suites pass with the changes, and regression\n  coverage for the fixed focus behavior is added where the repository's test framework\n  supports it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no\n  focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by the modal focus-trap fixes and\n  keyboard-operability remediation in Scope.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows:\n  covered by the focus-indicator consistency work in Scope; bundled with HLR-1 because\n  it applies to the same four UI surfaces and the same audit defect list, and is not\n  separately schedulable from the operability fixes on those surfaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29817,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aea6c24b1176351a","agent_id":"a22307e7dbf2d1113","session_id":"85349235-cd13-47e8-af33-caa47bbf874d","uuid":"7c0dddf6-0470-4c2e-9c36-7d57be148592","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:17:06.959Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
