{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbc5d6bbf2ebc1d8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the accessibility\n34\taudit in the four core Dashboard flows — project creation, workbench spawn, model\n35\tdeployment, and pipeline run submission — so that each flow is fully operable by\n36\tkeyboard alone, with no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and consistent visible\n37\tfocus indicators. This is the code-level deliverable of the keyboard accessibility\n38\tconformance strategy; the published conformance documentation that reflects this fixed\n39\tstate is handled separately by the documentation work stream.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Fix focus loss and focus traps in modals encountered across the four audited flows\n44\t  (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment, pipeline run submission).\n45\t- Make every control reachable and operable in those flows via keyboard alone,\n46\t  resolving each unreachable-control defect enumerated in the audit report.\n47\t- Apply a consistent, visible focus indicator pattern across all controls in the four\n48\t  audited flows, aligning to the correct indicator styling already present in parts of\n49\t  the console so the indicators are uniform.\n50\t- Resolve or explicitly disposition every defect item the audit report lists for the\n51\t  four flows.\n52\t- Incidental documentation touch-ups that fall out of these fixes (e.g., updated\n53\t  screenshots or references in existing Dashboard docs) are included here; substantive\n54\t  conformance content authoring (VPAT, accessibility statement) is out of this epic.\n55\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require, and any\n56\t  flow outside the four audited ones.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Each of the four audited flows can be completed end-to-end using only the keyboard,\n61\t  verified by a per-flow walkthrough of the audit defect list, with no focus traps and\n62\t  no unreachable controls.\n63\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for the four flows is resolved, or\n64\t  explicitly dispositioned with a recorded reason where the audit item is deemed not a\n65\t  defect.\n66\t- Focus indicators are visible and stylistically consistent across all interactive\n67\t  controls in the audited flows.\n68\t- The Dashboard's existing automated test suites pass with the changes, and regression\n69\t  coverage for the fixed focus behavior is added where the repository's test framework\n70\t  supports it.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with no\n75\t  focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by the modal focus-trap fixes and\n76\t  keyboard-operability remediation in Scope.\n77\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited flows:\n78\t  covered by the focus-indicator consistency work in Scope; bundled with HLR-1 because\n79\t  it applies to the same four UI surfaces and the same audit defect list, and is not\n80\t  separately schedulable from the operability fixes on those surfaces.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c55d8483d1c683","agent_id":"a029a4ff05a08bbb9","session_id":"85349235-cd13-47e8-af33-caa47bbf874d","uuid":"b6256812-9237-4799-bc54-1d0a377b9ed2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:18:10.129Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbc5d6bbf2ebc1d8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
