ince no unknown's resolution would change downstream structure. No `gated_by` is set\nanywhere, so no `gate_failure_impact` requirements are triggered; no epic lists an\nInvestigation in `dependencies`.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nBoth epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (not\n`investigation_signals`). E001's values check out against the strategy: the audit\nenumerates defects per flow (change_specificity 1), inconsistent indicators imply an\nin-codebase conforming pattern (pattern_precedent 1), the Open Questions section is\nempty (open_questions 1), and repo_access is corroborated by the architecture context\n(opendatahub-io/odh-dashboard upstream). The `architecture_claims: 1` on E001 is\nproperly calibrated — the rationale cites\n`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` corroborating the\nDashboard's role, which I verified exists and matches. E002's\n`human_process_gates: -1` is justified by HLR-3's explicit technical-review\nrequirement, and its `architecture_claims: 0` is sound because no architecture-context\nfile covers the Documentation component (verified: only dashboard.md exists under\nrhoai-3.0). Signal rationale files are present for both epics and match the\nfrontmatter values.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nE001's four ACs are testable (per-flow keyboard walkthrough against the audit defect\nlist, defect dispositioning, indicator consistency, test-suite pass plus added\nregression coverage). E002's ACs are testable and include the rule-mandated\ntechnical-review AC with recorded sign-off before republication. No replacement epic\nexists (remediation of existing flows, not a component replacement), so the\nrollback/feature-flag AC does not apply; no konflux-chain epic exists, so the build\npipeline AC does not apply. No AC states an externally-controlled precondition — the\ntechnical review is work the epic obtains and records, and all other ACs condition\nwhat the ep